This confirms both the new behavior and that no existing tests were broken by the change.,Documentation acceptance criterion is met by the expanded function-level documentation in src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts, which explicitly describes inline-code/backtick filtering:

"This function trims whitespace, strips any inline code spans wrapped in
backticks (replacing them with spaces of equal length to preserve character
boundaries), keeps any annotation tags that appear later in the line, and
supports common JSDoc styles such as leading "*".

It detects @story, @req, and @supports tags while preserving the rest
of the line for downstream logic."

Additional inline comments above the filtering logic further explain why the spaces are length-preserving and how this supports downstream annotation detection. This aligns with the story’s requirement to document the normalization behavior including inline code filtering.
